      "writtenOn": "2019-10-31T00:52:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to the API documentation, \nPreviewPrograms.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID and WatchNextPrograms.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID is a public ID of the content which allows an application to apply the same operation to all the preview program copies in different channels.\nIt means that PreviewPrograms.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID and WatchNextPrograms.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID can be a locally unique ID for the specific application (not globally unique, not URI format).\n \nOn the other hand, \nChannels.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID and Programs.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID introduced in this CL are globally unique URI.\n \nThis is one of the difference and reason why Channels.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID and Programs.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID cannot be consolidated with PreviewProgramColumns.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID.\n \nAlso, in case of considering to move COLUMN_CONTENT_ID from PreviewProgramColumns to BaseTvColumns, we need to consider if COLUMN_CONTENT_IDs are really necessary for RecordedPrograms and WatchedPrograms.\n \nSony thinks that adding RecordedPrograms.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID which is same definition as Programs.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID is an appropriate improvement. So, Sony will update the CL if you agree with this.\n(@Nick, @Sungsoo Would you let me know your opinion?)\n\nBut at least adding WatchedPrograms.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID is not neccesary since a system application can get it from Channels.COLUMN_CONTENT_ID specified by WatchedPrograms.COLUMN_CHANNEL_ID.\n\nThis is another reason why we should not move COLUMN_CONTENT_ID from PreviewProgramColumns to BaseTvColumns.",
